1:# Run book — Kartenzeit (Cloudflare Workers site)
13:- No Cloudflare credentials are needed for local development or validation
20:| `npm install` | installs `wrangler` (the only dev dependency) |
22:| `npm run build` | validation step: wrangler config, asset references, module syntax, data schema |
24:| `npm run check` | `build` + `test` + `wrangler deploy --dry-run` |
31:## Cloudflare Workers deployment
37:Wrangler configuration ([`wrangler.jsonc`](../wrangler.jsonc)):
56:### Build settings for Cloudflare (Workers Builds → “Connect Git repository”)
60:| Root directory | `/` (repository root) |
61:| Build command | `npm run build` (or `npm ci && npm run build`) |
62:| Deploy command | `npx wrangler deploy` (Workers Builds runs this from the root) |
67:beyond `ASSETS`, so no KV/D1/R2/secret setup is needed. Cloudflare performs the
80:`wrangler.jsonc` instead of a filesystem.
190:`public/_headers` (a Cloudflare Workers static-assets feature) sets
261:- **`wrangler dev` port in use** – `npx wrangler dev --port 8788`.
=== wrangler.jsonc ===
{
  // Cloudflare Workers site: static assets from ./public + a small request
  // handler in src/worker/index.js for /api/* (allowlisted upstream proxy).
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "zurich-maps",
  "main": "src/worker/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2025-08-01",
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat"],
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./public",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "not_found_handling": "single-page-application",
    // Only /api/* reaches the Worker; everything else is served straight from
    // the asset store (fast path, no Worker invocation, no asset cost).
    "run_worker_first": ["/api/*"]
  },
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  },
  "dev": {
    "port": 8787
  }
}

